Now I understand the issue. The `SparseMatrix.row_join` and `SparseMatrix.col_join` have special handling:

```python
if not self:
    return type(self)(other)
```

When `self` is a 0x0 matrix (i.e., "not self" is True because a 0x0 matrix is falsy), it returns `type(self)(other)` which is the other matrix itself. This bypasses the shape handling in `CommonMatrix.row_join`/`col_join`.

