The standard rotation matrix for a unit quaternion q = (a, b, c, d) (where a is scalar part, (b,c,d) is vector part):

m00 = 1 - 2(c² + d²)
m01 = 2(bc - ad)
m02 = 2(bd + ac)

m10 = 2(bc + ad)
m11 = 1 - 2(b² + d²)
m12 = 2(cd - ab)

